.Dd November 23, 2026
.Dt OSASCRIPT 1
.Os Minkar
.Sh NAME
.Nm osascript
.Nd run AppleScript
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l Ar language
.Op Fl e Ar statement ...
.Op Fl s Ar flags
.Op Ar programfile
.Op Ar argument ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
runs a script in AppleScript, given as
.Fl e
lines, a
.Ar programfile
or standard input, and prints its result.
The
.Ar argument Ns s
go to the script's
.Ic on run
handler.
Minkar's interpreter runs the commonly used part of the language:
values (numbers, text, lists, records), variables and properties,
.Ic if ,
.Ic repeat ,
.Ic try ,
handlers,
.Ic tell application ,
the text and list elements
.Pq Ic item , character , word , paragraph Ic of ,
and the commands
.Ic do shell script ,
.Ic display dialog ,
.Ic display notification ,
.Ic say ,
.Ic delay ,
.Ic beep ,
.Ic get volume settings ,
.Ic set volume ,
.Ic activate ,
.Ic quit ,
.Ic open .
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl e Ar statement
A line of the script; the option may be repeated.
.It Fl l Ar language
Only
.Cm AppleScript .
.It Fl s Ar flags
.Cm h :
the result readable (the default);
.Cm s :
as source, which could be compiled again;
.Cm o :
errors to standard output;
.Cm e :
errors to standard error (the default).
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0, or 1 after a syntax or execution error, printed as
.Dq Ar start Ns : Ns Ar end Ns : syntax error: Ar message Pq Ar number .
